          "title": "Hoc Mazarin",
          "subtitle": "Gambling",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hoc Mazarin is a historical French gambling game of the stops family, associated with the court of Versailles and Cardinal Mazarin."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hoc Mazarin was popular in seventeenth-century France, with rules printed from the mid-1600s and repeated in later French game books."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-3 players use the table arrangement described for Hoc Mazarin."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard French-suited pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard French-suited pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Prepare Standard French-suited pack and deal or lay out cards according to the documented Hoc Mazarin rules before play begins."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
